            <ArticleTitle>Palliative care pharmacotherapy literature summaries and analyses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>174-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/15360280902901404</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Timely and important studies are reviewed and commentaries provided by leading palliative care clinicians. Symptoms, interventions, and treatment-related adverse events addressed in this issue are computerized symptom management; anticholinergic agents in lung disease; neuropathic pain and morphine effectiveness; morphine dosing; inflammatory cytokines and pain; oral ghrelin-mimetics and sarcopenia; and opioid-induced bowel dysfunction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
